{% comment %}
  Renders the stand-in for a product that has no image yet, so cards and the product
  gallery keep the same footprint instead of collapsing.

  Must be a direct child of a `.media` element — base.css sizes it to fill the
  aspect-ratio box, and base.css centres the icon inside it.

  Usage:
  <div class="media media--transparent">{% render 'media-placeholder' %}</div>
{% endcomment %}

<div class="media-placeholder" role="img" aria-label="{{ 'products.product.media.no_image' | t }}">
  <svg
    class="media-placeholder__icon"
    viewBox="0 0 24 24"
    fill="none"
    stroke="currentColor"
    stroke-width="1.25"
    stroke-linecap="round"
    stroke-linejoin="round"
    aria-hidden="true"
    focusable="false"
  >
    {%- comment -%}
      Every shape clears the frame — a mountain line that meets or crosses the border
      doubles the stroke at the junction and reads as a smudge at card size.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <rect x="3" y="4.75" width="18" height="14.5" rx="2" />
    <circle cx="8.25" cy="9.75" r="1.25" />
    <path d="M6 16.5 9.75 12.5l2.75 2.9 2.25-1.9L18 16.5" />
  </svg>
</div>
